---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import SDriveVisual from '../components/SDriveVisual.astro';
import ProfilePhoto from '../components/ProfilePhoto.astro';
import SelectedWork from '../components/SelectedWork.astro';
import ProjectInvitation from '../components/ProjectInvitation.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Independent Product Engineer"><section class="section hero"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Independent thinking. Complete delivery.</span><h1>From your idea.<br/>To a business<br/><em>that runs.</em></h1><p class="lead">The apps, website, and systems your business needs to launch and run.</p><p class="hero-intro">I’m Minhaj, an independent product engineer. I build connected software for founders and businesses—from customer apps and websites to admin panels, backends, and cloud deployment.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/contact">Discuss your project ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href="/portfolio">View my work →</a></div><p class="hero-note">8+ years in mobile engineering · One accountable delivery partner</p></div><ProfilePhoto priority /></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Built around your business</span><h2>Where are you starting?</h2><p class="lead">Good software starts with understanding what you need to accomplish.</p></div><div class="grid"><article class="card"><span class="number">01 / AN IDEA</span><h3>You’re ready to launch.</h3><p>Turn the product in your head into a practical first release, with a clear scope and a connected build.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="number">02 / A BUSINESS</span><h3>Your operations need to connect.</h3><p>Give customers and your team the tools to book, manage, and deliver your service in one connected system.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="number">03 / AN EXISTING PRODUCT</span><h3>You’re ready for what’s next.</h3><p>Add capabilities, improve your mobile experience, or extend the software your business already relies on.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section services-section"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">How I can help</span><h2>One partner.<br/>The whole product.</h2><p class="lead">Direct communication with the person building your software. Connected decisions across your product and operations.</p><a class="text-link" href="/services">Explore services →</a></div><div class="service-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Launch a new product</h3><p>Planning, first-release scope, apps or web, backend, admin tools, and deployment.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Build your business platform</h3><p>Customer and provider experiences connected to your team’s workflows.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Improve an existing product</h3><p>New features, mobile development, integrations, and maintenance.</p></div></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section dark"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Flagship case study / SDrive</span><h2>A ride-hailing business.<br/>A connected platform.</h2><p class="lead">Riders, drivers, and administrators need different tools that work together. I independently delivered the rider and driver apps, marketing website, administration portal, backend, and cloud deployment.</p><div class="scope-tags"><span>Rider + driver apps</span><span>Website + admin</span><span>Backend + cloud</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/portfolio/sdrive">Explore the SDrive story →</a></div></div><SDriveVisual compact /></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Selected work</span><h2>Different businesses.<br/>Real product experience.</h2><p class="lead">A multi-role education product, a marketplace, and an operational tool—each with a clearly defined delivery scope.</p></div><SelectedWork /><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/portfolio">View all work →</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section process-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Working together</span><h2>A clear path from plan to launch.</h2></div><div class="process"><article><span class="eyebrow">01 / Understand</span><h3>Start with the business.</h3><p>Clarify users, workflows, and the problem the product needs to solve.</p></article><article><span class="eyebrow">02 / Plan</span><h3>Agree on the first release.</h3><p>Define scope, dependencies, milestones, and an estimate.</p></article><article><span class="eyebrow">03 / Build</span><h3>Review real progress.</h3><p>Build through reviewable milestones and demonstrate the connected experience.</p></article><article><span class="eyebrow">04 / Launch</span><h3>Prepare for real use.</h3><p>Test the system, deploy, and agree on handover and ongoing support.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Experience behind the delivery</span><h2>Technical depth.<br/>Personal accountability.</h2><p class="lead">My foundation is eight-plus years building Android and Flutter products, working with startups and remote teams across Dubai and Germany.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about">Get to know me →</a></div><div><blockquote class="quote">“Whether delivering as a solo developer or contributing to a team, he consistently produces exceptional results. He is my go-to person for any mobile product.”</blockquote><p class="muted">Yahya K. · Mobile development recommendation</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/minhaj-nadeem/details/recommendations/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read LinkedIn recommendations ↗</a><details><summary>How do we agree on scope?</summary><p>We clarify workflows and the first release before estimating the build. Complex projects can begin with a paid discovery phase.</p></details><details><summary>What about ownership and ongoing support?</summary><p>Source code handover, account ownership, third-party costs, and post-launch support are discussed and agreed as part of the project scope.</p></details></div></div></section><ProjectInvitation /></SiteLayout>
<style>.hero{padding:70px 0 74px}.hero h1 em{font-style:normal;color:#2f9983}.hero-intro{max-width:580px;color:#6b7280;font-size:.98rem}.hero-note{font-size:.75rem;color:#6b7280;margin-top:24px;margin-bottom:0}.services-section,.process-section{background:#f7f0f0}.service-list article{display:flex;gap:24px;border-top:1px solid #2f998333;padding:22px 0}.service-list article>span{font-size:.8rem;color:#2f9983;padding-top:16px}.service-list p{color:#6b7280;margin:0}.scope-tags{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px}.scope-tags span{border:1px solid #587c74;border-radius:4px;font-size:.75rem;padding:6px 10px}

</style>
